# Copied from scripts/kasr/extract/.gitignore's pattern. OCR and render
# caches, not results — regenerable from the corpus PDFs, and megabytes of
# machine output. `pagetext/` is the per-page text of every PDF, written by
# pagetext.py; `parts/` and `raw/` are per-file intermediates any extractor
# may use. The JSON result files beside them are tracked, because a batch
# that cites a page number should be checkable against what the page said.
pagetext/
parts/
raw/
__pycache__/
status-*.json

# Rendered pages — answer-key recovery rasterises pages to find highlights
# that exist only as pixels. Regenerable from the PDFs.
*.png
*.ppm
*.jpg
